\title{baystability: Bayesian Stability Analysis of Genotype by Environment Interaction (GEI)}
\description{
\pkg{baystability} implements the general Bayesian estimation method of linear-bilinear models of
Perez-Elizalde, Jarquin and Crossa (2012) for multi-environment trials: the AMMI model and the sites regression
(SREG, GGE) model, with the data of an earlier trial as the prior or with vague priors. Every parameter has a
posterior distribution, so the biplot carries inference: highest posterior density (HPD) regions show which
genotypes and environments interact significantly. For Bayesian stability analysis in general (Finlay-Wilkinson,
Eberhart-Russell and Shukla models, stability indices, probabilities of superior performance) see the package
\pkg{bayesstability}; for the Bayesian AMMI model of Crossa et al. (2011) see \pkg{bayesammi}.
}
\details{
\strong{Functions}, in the order of an analysis:
\itemize{
  \item \code{\link{bys_ls_means}}, \code{\link{bys_ls_var}}, \code{\link{bys_ls_gen_effects}},
    \code{\link{bys_ls_env_effects}}, \code{\link{bys_ls_ge_effects}}: cell means and variances, main effects,
    interaction effects and their singular value decomposition.
  \item \code{\link{bys_ls_ammi}}, \code{\link{bys_ls_model}}: least-squares AMMI and the mixed model of the
    error variance.
  \item \code{\link{bys_priors}}, \code{\link{bayes_ammi}}: vague priors and the Gibbs sampler, with an earlier
    trial as prior (\code{.prior_data}).
  \item \code{\link{bayes_ammi_biplot}}: the biplot with HPD regions.
  \item \code{\link{bys_compare}}: DIC and WAIC of several fits (for example numbers of terms).
  \item \code{\link{bys_interpret}}, \code{\link{bys_cite}}: a plain-language interpretation and the references of a
    result.
  \item \code{\link{bys_contrasts}}, \code{\link{bys_orthonormal}}: orthonormal contrasts and Gram-Schmidt
    orthonormalisation.
}
Every analysis returns the named list documented on its help page, with a class and methods (\code{print},
\code{summary}, \code{plot}, \code{as.data.table}); see \code{\link{bys-methods}}. Utilities:
\code{\link{bys_theme}}, \code{\link{bys_save}}, \code{\link{bys_notation}}, \code{\link{bys_reference}}.

\strong{Data.} \code{\link{cultivo2008}}, \code{\link{cultivo2009}}: grain yield of 12 maize hybrids in 25
environments in two years (Perez-Elizalde et al. 2012).

\strong{Vignettes.} Start with \code{vignette("baystability_01_getting_started", package = "baystability")};
\code{browseVignettes("baystability")} lists all of them, each as HTML and as PDF.
}
